(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology on July 5, 2018 showed a video of the growth of water resources in Cambodia, such as: rivers, streams, lakes, natural water, groundwater and seawater. Serving agriculture, handicrafts, power industry, navigation, culture, tourism and ecosystem support.
In the video, it is revealed that today, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has installed the Techo Sen Radar Station for effective climate control for forecasting operations within a radius of 400 km, which can monitor the evolution of the weather. .
In addition, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has set up automatic meteorological stations and automatic hydrological stations in major rivers, streams and rivers to obtain specific weather data related to water level and water resources for forecasting meteorological conditions and conditions. Regular and accurate hydrology and timely dissemination to the public of natural disasters such as: droughts, hurricanes, lightning and floods.
Currently, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has installed 38 automatic hydrological stations in the Mekong, Tonle Sap and Tonle Bassac rivers, as well as 35 automatic meteorological stations in the capitals and provinces.
