Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the 18 factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen today were invested by 21 Chinese factories and 1 Korean factory. , 1 factory in Japan and 2 factories in Cambodia. These 25 factories have 21 garment factories, 3 bag factories and 1 embroidery factory.
According to Ith Sam Heng, the products produced by these factories are exported to international markets and also supplied to domestic markets.
The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training confirmed that factories based in Ang Snoul district and from nearby districts have created many additional jobs and jobs that make it easier for young people to find work in their locality. Renting houses, selling food, transportation and other services contribute to the economic development and livelihood of local people.
According to the minister, there are currently 462 factories, enterprises and establishments in Kandal province with 150,515 workers with a total wage of $ 363 million. There are 168 garment and footwear factories with 134,323 workers with a total wage of more than 322 million US dollars.
Please note that the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and workers in Kandal province today is the 49th meeting since August 20, 2017. The 48 meetings were attended by a total of 681,633 workers.
