Hot! Afghan military "kills 132 militants" in both ground and air strikes!
KABUL (Reuters) - At least 132 militants have been killed and 28 others injured in a deadly military and air operation in Afghanistan since Tuesday. This is according to the Ministry of Defense of Afghanistan, quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday evening, July 4, 2018.
According to a statement from the Afghan Ministry of Defense, its ground forces have launched nearly 100 military operations, both large and small, in 15 of Afghanistan's 34 provinces.
The Afghan Air Force also launched airstrikes on militants during the same period. However, there was no confirmation on the number of casualties on the part of the security forces.
The Afghan military and the NATO-led coalition have stepped up ground and air operations against the militants in recent months as militants have launched more frequent attacks. Across the country. National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia Holds Second Job Fair to Promote Employment Development
