At the same time, Mr. Miyama Masahiro pledged to promote Cambodia's investment opportunities and potential to the business community in Japan in order to attract more Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia's SME and other priority sectors to contribute to The Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing poverty and promoting national economic growth. The United States celebrates the 242nd National Independence Day on July 4, 2018!
Independence Day, or National Day, July 4, is a holiday throughout the United States to celebrate the independence of this great power on July 4, 1776. More than 240 years ago, the 13 American colonies declared themselves an independent nation called the United States, which meant that they were no longer under the yoke of British colonial rule.
From then on, every July 4, celebrations, mostly through fireworks, parades, barbecues, gatherings and baseball games, were held. Others also celebrate this special day by creating public and private events that celebrate the history, government, and traditions of the American people.
However, the term "Independence Day" was not used until 1791.
