The largest rice warehouse and drying shed in Kampong Thom province with a capital of 5 million dollars, officially inaugurated!
(Kampong Thom): The largest warehouse of 50,000 tons of rice and 1,500 tons of rice per day in Kampong Thom province with a capital of 5 million dollars was officially inaugurated by Amru Rice Company this morning. July 4, 2018.
The 50,000-tonne rice warehouse and 1,500-tonne-per-day rice mill are being built under a special investment project in the form of a $ 5 million debt owed by the Royal Government of Cambodia to Amru Rice.
He said that at the same time, in order to solve the problem of large-scale rice warehouses and rice mills, the Royal Government has set up a special intervention mechanism in the form of debt, allowing the private sector to receive projects to operate the construction of rice warehousing and rice mills have sufficient capacity to absorb The rice of the people in this area is the high consideration of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
During the growing season, through the Agricultural Productivity Increase Project, the Royal Government subsidizes the price of rice seeds for farmers at about 1,000 riels per kilogram, which means that if rice producers sell at 3,000 riels per kilogram, the state Will help out 1,000 Riels, farmers out only 2,000 Riels.
Mr. Kao Thach is confident that this year's harvest season, through a large rice warehouse and rice dryer, is a new achievement in Kampong Thom province that has sufficient capacity to absorb rice from local farmers and ensure The market price of rice, as well as help solve the problem of damage to your rice.
He added that in addition to large-scale rice warehousing and drying facilities, the Royal Government of Cambodia has also taken into account the long-term security of rice prices, in order to reduce production costs and farmers' transportation costs to become more marketable. More.
Mr. Ros Silva, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance, Representative of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, said that through the Rural Development Bank, the operator of the Royal Government's special projects, it has been implemented effectively through the storage mechanism. Dry rice stocks will be provided as a working capital of the mill owner to provide credit to the mill for purchasing rice during the harvest season.
He added that the mechanism maintains affordable prices for farmers and fills a sufficient supply of rice for export. In fact, the price of rice of farmers across the country increased significantly in 2017-2018, especially fragrant rice, which is 1,200 riel / kg.
Mr. Ros Silva requested the local authorities to facilitate the purchase and sale of rice as well as other agricultural products by facilitating the transportation of rice from the fields or gathering places to buy and sell rice at the commune hall or other convenient places. To collect and buy and sell farmers. This reduces the cost of rice collectors, reduces the role of brokers, which increases the benefits to farmers by increasing the cost of leaving the fields or farms.
He added that the installation of 50,000 tons of rice warehouses and 1,500 tons of rice dryers in Kampong Thom province has effectively contributed to solving farmers' concerns, especially the unreasonable fall in rice prices.
According to the latest data from the Chinese Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, in the first five months of 2018, the total mobile Internet data flow reached 21 billion gigabytes. Of that, 20.6 billion gigabytes of data flow came from mobile phones. Total mobile internet data flow during this period increased by 196% compared to the same period last year. Data flow from mobile phones increased by 212 percent.
Part of this growth may be due to the government's commitment to reducing the cost of mobile internet services. As of July 1, the three major telecom operators will abolish roaming charges for local data and reduce roaming charges for home internet as well as international roaming. With less cost, more users will be able to access the internet on a daily basis.
Online shopping has grown dramatically this year, with online retail sales from January to May rising more than 30 percent to $ 500,000.
Other forms of IT use, such as mobile payments, video streaming and new media, are also on the rise.
New products such as smart city systems, virtual glasses, driverless cars, wearable devices and drones are all things that rely heavily on mobile internet. Experts say these products will be the most advanced products in the use of information technology in China. (China's CCTV)
