(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and China have cooperated on environmental protection by expanding the scope and analysis capacity of air, water and soil quality, which will help improve the environment in Cambodia, especially Phnom Penh.
Three documents on the agreement on environmental cooperation, including: the establishment of the Cambodia-China Environmental Cooperation Center, the Cambodia-China Biodiversity Conservation Cooperation and the project to support wastewater treatment plants, were signed by a memorandum of understanding. Senior officials of the Ministry of Environment of Cambodia and the Ministry of Environment of China on July 4, 2018.
ZHAO Yingmin, China's Deputy Minister of Ecology and Environment, said the cooperation focused on air pollution, water pollution and soil pollution, in which the Chinese side could share experiences and provide relevant information. Respond to the need for solving environmental problems in Cambodia.
He added that this is a good cooperation of the Royal Government of Cambodia - China to jointly address environmental issues, ecosystems and biodiversity that have been polluted by development and climate change.
