Today, General Mak Chito and Stung Treng Provincial Prosecutor burn more than 30 kilograms of drugs
(Stung Treng): Drugs including: methamphetamine and more than 31 kilograms of narcotics were set on fire this morning, July 4, 2018, in the presence of General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police for drug planning. And Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of Stung Treng Provincial Court, which took place in front of Stung Treng Provincial Hall, with the participation of professional officers of the Armed Forces and relevant authorities.
On this occasion, General Mak Chito said, "Stung Treng is not a drug-producing province, but one of the most affected because criminals take the territory of this province to bring drugs through."
Yong Sovathana, deputy governor and director of the provincial anti-drug secretariat, said trade, storage, distribution, use and trafficking of drugs through Stung Treng still occur.
He added that within a year, the provincial secretariat has set up drug control committees in communes to increase outreach and education programs to be multidisciplinary everywhere.
Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of Stung Treng Provincial Court, also said, "We must continue to work together to deepen the dissemination rules and the monitoring mechanism at the commune level, the coordination committee, the guardians and the community must work together." "In multidisciplinary, increasing publicity is better than cracking down."
He stated that the drug problem has ruined the future of the children and caused social insecurity, and the suspects who secretly kept, traded and used us to crack down are only cheaters at the instigation of the mastermind, so the education mechanism Leaving school will be effective.
At the same time, the representatives of teachers of the Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports confirmed that the education officials have also set up educational groups to educate about the effects of accidents and the law on drug control in educational institutions that have been implemented on a regular basis. And this understanding in the past has made some of our young people change themselves into one of the best.
It should be noted that the drugs burned today include: methamphetamine (white gram powder), more than 31 kilograms, 29 ice cubes, more than 1933 tablets and other exhibits.
