(Koh Kong): Eleven workers of Koh Kong Special Economic Zone who work for Yasaki Company fainted at midnight on July 4, 2018 at the power plant in Koh Kong Odd Area in Pak Klang Commune. Mondul Seima, Koh Kong Province.
Workers who fainted were taken by the company to the Provincial Referral Hospital overnight, and the cause of the fainting was due to the electric current and the smell of the electric wire, so they fainted.
Mr. Yok Sangvat, Director of the Provincial Department of Labor, said this morning, July 4, that the cause of the 11 workers fainted due to the electric shock caused them to smell and they lost the smell and fainted. Not as much as before, and the company immediately transported the workers to the provincial referral hospital.
Dr. Hay Laysun, director of the Provincial Referral Hospital, said that the factory workers who fainted were treated by doctors with care, there was no negligence because the doctors performed their duties. Physicians, professional ethics and compliance with the regulations of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health.
The doctor added that the workers who are being treated in the 11 hospitals are not required to pay for their services and are under the care of our doctors and arrived this morning. That the 11 workers have some relief. Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at a Conversation with Nearly 30,000 Workers in Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province
(Kandal): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Wednesday morning, July 4, 2018, met with 27,427 workers from Cambodia. 18 factories in Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
* As a start, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure to meet with the workers today.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told workers that if the CPP wins the election, Samdech will continue to meet with workers, but on the contrary, if the CPP does not win the election, Samdech will not have the opportunity to meet with workers. No more. However, Samdech still expects that the workers will continue to vote for Samdech to vote for the Cambodian People's Party.
Through the workers in this morning's conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked their grandparents for their joint efforts to help the nation and the Royal Government recover from the difficult situation.
* Samdech Techo stated that the bus has been launched to Ang Snoul district, so workers can use the public bus service of Phnom Penh Capital Hall for free for at least 2 more years.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, is considering connecting buses outside Phnom Penh, especially in the factory area, so that workers can use this bus for free.
* Samdech Prime Minister stated that Samdech has made efforts from a country that lacks rice to become a country of rice and export rice abroad.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has done a lot of work in the agricultural sector and has also been successful, reaching the stage of food shortage until the rest of the rice to sell abroad.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Royal Government has made efforts to deploy sugar factories, cassava factories to collect sugarcane and potatoes for farmers, and the Royal Government has also invested in rice mills and invested capital to buy rice from the people.
* Samdech Techo emphasizes that the Royal Government has made great efforts to promote this agricultural sector, and Cambodia's agriculture today is not the agriculture of the Pol Pot regime.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has been paying attention to the processing industry for processing Cambodia's agricultural products for export.
* Samdech Techo stated that during the ruling CPP, there was no policy of taxing farmers' farmland.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that industry in the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era flourished but was destroyed by the flames of war, especially after the March 18, 1970 coup.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that currently there are more than 100 factories in the garment and footwear sector, with more than 800,000 workers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to bring the country to the stage it is now, it is important to rely on peace, this peace is to give confidence to investors and tourists.
* The Prime Minister stated that Cambodia has already gone through the ravages of war in the past, so we must continue to work together to maintain peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to maintain peace, it is easy to vote for the Cambodian People's Party to support Samdech Techo as Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on factory owners to pay attention to the well-being of workers by creating appropriate dining areas and other treatment facilities. At the same time, the factory owners take care of the workers, they also have to work hard. Samdech stated that when the factory owners get profit, the workers also have higher wages.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is a country left with many widows and orphans due to the fires of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people living with HIV not to spread the virus to others, this call after seeing signs of a resurgence of HIV, which requires attention.
* Samdech Techo, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that whether Cambodia grows or not depends on the people, do you vote for the CPP or not?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in addition to visiting workers in the garment and footwear industry, there are also workers in other sectors, such as hotel construction.
* Samdech Techo stated that Samdech will end his work when other parties win the election, but Samdech believes that no political party can compete with the CPP.
