(Phnom Penh): Mr. Osman Hassan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, intervened on a worker named Ken Chantha who cheated a recruiter and sent her to work illegally in Saudi Arabia for more than a year. 4 years illegally.
The intervention comes in response to a request for help from the worker on Facebook, which described the origins of being tricked into becoming a domestic worker in Saudi Arabia. Labor, harassment from employers, and non-payment of salaries.
On the afternoon of July 3, 2018, Mr. Osman Hassan confirmed that the victim was very happy while on a flight from Judea, Saudi Arabia to Bangkok to continue the journey back to Cambodia. Arriving at Phnom Penh International Airport on the morning of July 4 tomorrow.
Mr. Osman Hassan stated that "a Cambodian worker named Ken Chantha was born in Wat Bo village, Siem Reap commune, Siem Reap district, Siem Reap province, who went to work as a housemaid in Saudi Arabia for more than four years, cheating the brokers. "I, on behalf of the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, to help her return to Cambodia, will arrive in Cambodia tomorrow morning, July 4, on a Bangkok PG flight."
According to Osman Hassan, this is the fourth victim he has managed to return to Cambodia because there are no embassies or consulates in the Arab world.
Please be informed that the first time he cooperated with the Cambodian Embassy in Kuwait and Egypt, and the second time, the third, the fourth time cooperated with the Cambodian Embassy in Egypt.
