During the three days from July 1 to 3, the police inspected a total of 3,490 vehicles and found 627 offending vehicles, 265 education vehicles and 362 fines. The Minister of Agriculture announces the dissemination and implementation of guidelines on the Ministry's public financial reform monitoring and evaluation system.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 3, was invited to announce the launch and implementation of the Guidelines on the Monitoring and Evaluation Planning System Prepared by the Financial Reform Working Group. Ministry of Public Works in collaboration with the Department of Planning and Statistics.
This program aims to disseminate and implement guidelines to increase the efficiency of public financial management reform, as well as to promote good governance and transparency in the management of the national budget, especially the expenditures that will be improved, management and accountability. There is a standard for the efficient use of budget resources, both current and capital.
The Minister also made some important recommendations to reform the public finances in accordance with the Rectangular Strategy, the National Strategic Development Plan and the Agricultural Development Strategic Plan, including:
2. All budget units, both at the central and provincial levels, must pay attention to the preparation and implementation of the budget plan within the framework of the budget in a good and effective manner based on the guidelines on the monitoring and evaluation planning system.
3. The head of the budget unit must have a sense of responsibility in the ownership of the management and implementation of its budget to be transparent, efficient and effective. The monitoring and evaluation planning system requires the appointment of responsible leaders and officials, so all budget units must appoint competent officers to operate the system, especially officers who understand information technology in computerized monitoring and evaluation.
4. In order to strengthen the effective implementation of this guideline, the Internal Audit Department and the Planning and Statistics Department must thoroughly monitor this work in order to ensure that all budget units implement budget planning, monitoring and evaluation in the appropriate format. Introduced this.
5. The Strategic Budget Plan is a mechanism for the annual budgeting process, which is implemented within the framework of the implementation of the public financial reform program and the strategic direction of the budget system reform that each ministry, institution and budget unit Must be properly organized, transparent and accountable in implementing the policies of the Ministry and the National Strategic Development Plan.
