(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the Prime Minister of Cambodia after liberating the genocidal regime of Pol Pot since 1985. Until now, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been the Prime Minister for 33 years.
Although after the 1993 election, Samdech Techo Hun Sen served as the second Prime Minister for five years, the decision on the fate of the nation remained in the hands of the same Samdech. Many Cambodians saw the progress of the nation and were amazed at the leadership of the country by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, but some also expressed dissatisfaction with some points.
Despite serving as Prime Minister for 33 years, working for Cambodia between 1985 and 1998 was still a period of crisis in the internal armed conflict, so at this stage Cambodia's development has not been successful. Better yet.
The teacher, who is teaching at Borey 100 High School, said that he came to live in Sen Sok district during 1993. He said that the Sen Sok area in 1993 was all rice fields, not areas with high-rise buildings like today.
He expressed his satisfaction with the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, although the current economic situation in Cambodia is not as strong as some other countries. He said that although Samdech Techo Hun Sen had the opportunity to lead the country for 33 years, the promotion of national development was only in the last 20 years.
A young woman studying at Borey 100 High School also expressed her satisfaction with the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. According to the young woman, her parents have been living in Sen Sok for more than 10 years.
She reminded that the Sen Sok area more than 10 years ago is not like today, which is rich in residential and commercial buildings, mostly only rice fields. She also saw the progress of infrastructure systems in Phnom Penh, such as roads and flyovers, which is a demonstration of progress in Phnom Penh.
The young woman who has just reached the age of voting in 2018 has expressed her satisfaction with the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and she will continue to support Samdech Techo as Prime Minister through the upcoming election.
