China launches national campaign to crack down on real estate irregularities (Video inside) (China): China's Ministry of Housing and Rural Development will launch a national campaign this month to reduce illegal practices. Of real estate agents and real estate developers, as well as to standardize the real estate market in China.
According to a statement issued by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Development of China and six central government departments, 30 cities, including Beijing, Shanghai and Guangzhou, will be inspected for property irregularities. The inspection began on July 2 and will end at the end of December.
The censorship will refer to irregularities, including providing exaggerated information about home sales, fake advertisements, dishonest home price increases, market abuse and concealment of unsold homes.
Local authorities are required to take strong action against these practices, including the issuance of fake licenses and illegal mortgage methods.
The public is also encouraged to participate in this review.
Official data for June showed that house prices in most of China's major cities were stable in May as local governments tightened controls to curb expectations of rising house prices.
Home prices for new homes in the top four cities fell 0.6 percent last month, the fourth straight month in a row, according to the National Bureau of Statistics. From last year.
In recent years, soaring house prices in major cities have raised concerns about real estate risks. To curb speculation about raising house prices, local governments have tightened restrictions on home purchases and increased the deposit amount for mortgages.
In response, the government is implementing a long-term mechanism for real estate management that will ensure the sustainable and stable development of the real estate market.
The National Committee for Development and Reform of China and the Chinese Ministry of Finance have issued a joint statement on debt risk management, stating that bonds issued by overseas real estate companies should be used for debt repayment. Primarily.
