A family in Siem Reap who was desperate for life after their house was destroyed by fire turned into a smile immediately after receiving a house from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Siem Reap): General Chea Dara and the team of National Defense University visited Meanchey commune, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province on July 2, 2018 to hand over a house as a gift to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who has completed the construction for a family of 68-year-old Thap Sung in Daun Nom village, Meanchey commune, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province.
Thap Sung's house was completely destroyed by fire on the night of May 7, 2018. At that time, Thap Sung and his wife were desperate for a living because the house was completely destroyed, there was nothing left and no property in the house.
But things turned into a smile immediately after receiving the house from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit through General Chea Dara.
Both husband and wife said excitedly and with tears in their eyes that on the night of his house fire, he was hopeless and his wife fainted, but did not expect that in the morning the CPP team led by Chief General Chea Dara arrived at his house to bring emergency aid immediately.
The family of Grandpa Thap Soeng thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, and Mrs. and Mr. Chea Dara and the working group of the People's Party. Cambodia really lives with the people under all circumstances and they promise to go to the polls on July 29 to support the Cambodian People's Party.
