Samdech Techo Hun Sen: China's support is an important contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development (Video indise) (Phnom Penh): The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, expressed his satisfaction with China's support for Lead in Cambodia. Samdech stated that China's support for Cambodia is an important contribution to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks while presiding over the celebration of the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-China relations at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center on the evening of July 2, 2018.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia and China established formal diplomatic relations on July 19, 1958, after the first bilateral meeting between His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King and His Excellency Zhou Enlai, former Chinese Prime Minister. During the Bandung Conference in April 1955 in Bandung, Indonesia, and the reciprocal visits between the two countries' senior leaders during 1956.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia stated that this historic friendship was jointly built by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King and President Mao Zedong, Prime Minister Zhou Enlai, as well as previous generations of Chinese leaders. Continuous progress to become a comprehensive strategic partnership cooperation on December 13, 2010.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia highly values the Chinese government in respecting its independence, sovereignty and the Royal Government of Cambodia's measures to protect security and social stability. Cambodia congratulates on the positive results of the cooperation and the fruits of the past.
Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is committed to further enhance the scope of Cambodia-China comprehensive strategic partnership and cooperation for the benefit of the people of both countries.
