6 years, 1 million trees to be planted in the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park in Preah Vihear Province
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, outlined some visions to be implemented in the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park, in which the Royal Academy has set a goal to rebuild the forest cover with all kinds of trees. In the Kingdom of Cambodia, using 6 years to plant 1 million trees.
Dr. Sok Touch said that the Royal Academy of Cambodia has set the vision of the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trep, including:
1. Transform the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park into a park for research and development by linking theory to practice.
2. Rebuild forest cover with all kinds of trees in the Kingdom of Cambodia, using 6 years to plant 1 million trees.
3. Transform this area into three types of tourism areas: environmental tourism, cultural tourism and artificial tourism.
4. Transform this area into a document production area based on scientific research, writing books and producing videos to provide easy lessons and methods for farmers to implement to improve their living standards. And to contribute to making Cambodia a high middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050.
5. Transform the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Park into our garden and the world.
6. Organize the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park to provide employment to the people in this area and researchers with the same direction.
Meanwhile, Ms. Sagong Hee, Head of Land Policy Assessment of the Korea Environmental Institute (KEI), stated that over the years, the KEI Institute and the Royal Academy of Cambodia have joined hands to create a better environment in Cambodia, and she is very happy. From today, KEI of Korea and the Royal Academy of Cambodia can organize a series of joint work related to the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park.
