Official Cambodia-China relations were established on July 19, 1958, five years after Cambodia gained independence from France. The relationship comes just three years after His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk met with Chinese Prime Minister Zhou Inlay in Bandung, Indonesia, while attending a non-aligned conference. April 1955
Please be reminded that the Beijing government began to work closely with the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in 1997, especially after the first visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the so-called strong man. Cambodia went to China in 1999.
Starting from this visit, the Royal Government of Cambodia of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has become an important cooperation partner of China. Senior Cambodian-Chinese leaders have been in frequent contact with each other. In December 2010, Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid a visit to China, and the two countries further enhanced their strategic partnership.
China is the largest investor in Cambodia, according to data from the Council for the Development of Cambodia as of April 2018, Chinese investment in Cambodia totaled about 17 billion US dollars.
Human-cultural exchanges between the two countries are constantly expanding. The number of Chinese tourists in 2016 increased to 830,000, and as of August 2017, the number of Chinese tourists reached more than 1 million. Every day, 35 flights fly between China and Cambodia, and more than 10 Chinese cities have direct flights to Cambodia.
