(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior on July 2, 2018 issued a statement condemning Human Rights Watch (HRW) for fabricating false reports attacking 12 leaders of the Cambodian Armed Forces. At the same time, the Ministry of Interior, the competent ministry of Cambodia, also warned to take action against the fabrication of this false report.
A statement from the Ministry of Interior stated: "Human Rights Watch (HRW), headed by Brett Adams, often invents and develops so-called" crazy "human rights reports. "It is an insult to the progress in all areas of the Kingdom of Cambodia under the leadership of the legitimate government born of the election."
The Ministry of Interior also considered that the HRW report also reflected the corrupt tactics of a number of foreign groups with the idea of supporting traitorous Cambodian politicians with the aim of causing chaos and destroying the peace, stability and security of the Cambodian people.
The following is the statement of the Ministry of Interior: Important remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of celebrating the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-China relations at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit on Monday evening, July 2, 2018, presided over the congratulatory ceremony. 60th Anniversary of Cambodia-China Relations.
The event was held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center with the participation of Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Sung Por, senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders of the Cambodian-Chinese Association, as well as major Cambodian and Chinese investors. Many more.
As the beginning of his speech at the celebration of the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-China relations, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked his Chinese friends for their constant support in financial, technical, human resource training and infrastructure construction.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that China's support is an important contribution to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia and China established formal diplomatic relations on July 19, 1958, following the first bilateral meeting between His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King and former Prime Minister Zhou Enlai. China during the Bandung Conference in April 1955 in Bandung, Indonesia and the reciprocal visits between the two countries' top leaders during 1956.
* The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia stated that this historic friendship was jointly built by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King and President Mao Zedong, Prime Minister Zhou Enlai, as well as previous generations of Chinese leaders. Continued to develop into a comprehensive strategic partnership cooperation on December 13, 2010.
* Samdech Techo emphasized that in the past 60 years, the leaders of the two countries have always strived to maintain friendly relations and overcome many obstacles to lead the country and its people to progress, prosperity and harmony.
* Samdech Techo expressed confidence that the friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and China will contribute to building a community with a common destiny for all mankind, as Chinese President Xi Jinping recently said.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the official visit and co-chairs of the 2nd Mekong-Lanchang Summit of the Chinese Prime Minister Li Keqiang in Phnom Penh on January 10-11. Go is the opening of the celebration of the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations.
* The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia stated that in the tourism sector, there are 15 airlines operating regular flights between Cambodia and China. In 2017, there were about 1.2 million Chinese tourists. As of the first quarter of 2018, Cambodia received a total of 1.7 million international tourists, including more than 500,000 Chinese tourists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia highly values the Chinese government in respecting the independence, sovereignty and measures taken by the Royal Government of Cambodia for the promotion of security and social stability.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia congratulates the positive results of the cooperation and the fruits of the past.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is committed to further enhance the scope of Cambodia-China comprehensive strategic partnership and cooperation for the benefit of the people of both countries.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of July 2, 2018, met with Mr. Ma Yi, Director General of the Office of Fisheries Law Enforcement in Yangtze River to discuss the project. Cooperation on aquaculture development and fisheries resource management in Cambodia, Ministry of Agriculture.
On this occasion, Ma Yi thanked the Minister and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for their close cooperation with the Chinese Ministry of Agriculture. He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set the right policy to maintain a fishery yield of around 600,000 tons per year and promote aquaculture development.
At the same time, he made it clear that he would continue to deepen cooperation with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and planned to invite the ministry's leaders and officials to visit the development of new technologies and techniques for development. Aquaculture in China.
At the same time, the Director General of the Office of Enforcement of Fisheries Law on the Yangtze River also requested the Cambodian side to study the technical needs that Cambodia is lacking and asked Mr. Veng Sakhon to examine the possibility of support.
Ma Yi also said that the Mekong-Lanchang cooperation will boost the fishery stocks, capacity building, human resources and aquaculture production.
He also invited leaders of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to attend a forum on fisheries resource management and aquaculture development in October 2018 in Wuhan, People's Republic of China.
(Phnom Penh): Cambodians working in Thailand have informed Battambang Provincial MP Chheang Vun that they will come to the polls on July 29 to elect a democratic leader. .
Workers in Thailand have stated that this is an opportunity to exercise their rights to the fullest, without losing the grip of some unscrupulous people who have called for people not to go to the polls.
Please be informed that Mr. Chheang Vun, as the Chairman of the Task Force for the Relations of Cambodian Workers, led the team to meet and greet Cambodian workers who went to work in Thailand from June 29 and 30 to July 1. In 2018, the team met 1,750 Cambodian workers at four different locations in Ratchaburi, Thailand, 80% of whom left Battambang.
The representatives of the Cambodian workers thanked the CPP MPs for visiting them and stressed that on the upcoming election day, they will definitely go to the polls to vote for the CPP. Good MPs who care about the welfare of workers, especially elect leaders who have sacrificed their physical and mental strength to liberate the nation, build peace and develop the country to progress to this day.
At the same time, Mr. Chheang Vun expressed his deep gratitude for the right decision of the Cambodian workers working in Thailand who are highly willing to participate in promoting democracy and the rule of law in Cambodia. He asserted that the election was a democratic election under international law, unlike the former CNRP, which intended to overthrow the legitimate government under the color revolution to gain power on foreign orders.
