Cambodian Embassies in China and Malaysia Intervene to Help 14 Cambodians Return Home
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian embassies in China and Malaysia have intervened to help 14 Cambodians return home after they cheated brokers into marriage and work illegally.
In this case, the Embassy issued a letter of clearance and coordination with the Malaysian Immigration Office, and the nine Cambodians returned to Cambodia between 23 and 29 June 2018.
In the second case, the Cambodian Embassy in China cooperated with the Chinese authorities to intervene, rescue and repatriate five Cambodians from Kampong Cham, Takeo and Prey Veng provinces, four of whom were women. The broker was traveling from Cambodia to marry illegally in China, and another was the child of one of the victims.
The embassy provided accommodation and meals, as well as travel documents for the five Cambodians, and they returned to Cambodia on the night of June 28, 2018.
