(Siem Reap): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism Tith Chantha has expressed optimism that in the future, about 2 million Chinese tourists will come to Cambodia each year, or more than 2 million, and Cambodia will hold a big celebration. .
He made the remarks while presiding over a seminar on strengthening and expanding public-private cooperation in the field of Cambodia-China tourism on behalf of Minister Thong Khon at the Sokha Hotel in Siem Reap this morning. July 2018, with the participation of Mr. Zhang Xilong, Director General of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism of China, as part of the celebration of the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China.
He said that Cambodia is ready to receive Chinese tourists, such as the expansion of direct flights between Cambodia and China, the training of Chinese tour guides, the establishment of more tourist destinations for Chinese tourists, etc., with the most close diplomatic relations. Between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the People's Republic of China through the Belt and Road Policy and the Silk Road Policy initiated by Chinese President Xi Jinping.
The Secretary of State stressed that the increase in the number of Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia is like the flow of the Mekong River, which originates in China, and does not dry up in the sense of strengthening diplomatic ties, especially in the field of tourism.
He requested the Chinese Ministry of Culture and Tourism and the private tourism sector to continue good cooperation with Cambodia to promote the potential of Cambodian tourism in the Chinese market, training and capacity building of tourism officials and operators to better meet the needs of the Chinese market. .
This collaboration clearly reflects our sense of responsibility, our joint efforts and commitment to promoting sustainable and responsible tourism development, and actively contributes to accelerating and promoting Effective socio-economic growth.
