"Compared to the commune elections we did in the past, I think it is better now because it is quiet and the people are doing business normally. It means good peace, good stability, "Heng Vanda added.
The democratic process and elections in Cambodia were hard-won by senior Cambodian political figures, His Majesty Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, with foreign support until the 1993 elections. Since 1993, elections have been held steadily and continuously improved.
Proponents of her case have been working to make the actual transcript of this statement available online. Their campaign is seen as destroying the democracy in Cambodia that they are promoting.
Mr. Heng Vanda said, "In fact, democracy is propaganda for the people to go to the polls, but if the people are not allowed to go to the polls, it is a killer of democracy."
