(Pailin): Pailin is one of the 25 provinces / capitals in Cambodia, which is located in the northwest of the country, 371 km from Phnom Penh and 84 km from Battambang. There are two national roads from Phnom Penh to Pailin: National Road No. 5 to Battambang and from Battambang to Pailin is National Road No. 57.
Thanks to the efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he set out a win-win policy, using life as a capital to end the war that began in 1996 and was completely successful on December 29, 1998. That makes the armed forces of all tendencies come together in a single Cambodian society under the Constitution.
After the Pailin area achieved complete peace under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, this area, formerly part of Battambang province, was established as Pailin City. At the same time, Pailin province also has Phnom Yat cultural and historical tourism sites and many other natural resorts that attract national and international tourists to visit every year.
By 2018, the 5th mandate of the National Assembly of Pailin Province has achieved full peace for 20 years and has developed like the capitals and provinces throughout the country, in which the four priority areas set by Samdech Techo Hun Sen During the 1980s, the priority of the present is "water, electricity, human roads".
