Court orders detention of 5 suspects in connection with the crime of hiring a Cambodian woman to become a surrogate mother
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kor Vandy, Deputy Chief and Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, has decided to issue a temporary detention order for a group of 5 suspects involved in the crime of hiring a Cambodian woman to become a surrogate mother. The detention order was issued on the evening of June 28, 2018.
Phnom Penh Municipal Court spokesman Ly Sophanna confirmed that the five suspects were charged by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court with "cross-border human trafficking and intermediaries with pregnant women" under Article 16 of the law. Suppression of human trafficking and protection of minors and Article 332 of the Penal Code.
It should be reminded that the police force of the Office of Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors, in cooperation with the local police force, cracked down on human trafficking cases for cross-border trafficking and intermediary acts of surrogacy by detaining 5 male and female suspects and freeing the female victims. 33 accidents.
The operation to crack down on surrogacy took place on the evening of June 21, 2018, at Villa 2A, Street 348 and Villa 9A, Street 348, located in Borey Vimean Phnom Penh, along Street 5 in Sangkat Russey Keo. Russey Keo district, under the direct command of General Chuon Sovann, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Police Commissioner.
According to the police, the operation was coordinated by Mr. Kuch Kimlong, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and led by Brigadier General Chan Kittikhom, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. .
