Cambodia-EU trade volume is nearly 6 billion dollars, of which Cambodia exports more than 4 billion dollars, Europe is the largest importer of goods from Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The trade volume between Cambodia and the European Union was nearly 6 billion dollars in 2017, while Cambodia exported more than 4 billion dollars to Europe, while the European Union imported nearly 1 billion dollars to Cambodia. This is according to Ms. Tek Reth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
Speaking at the first European Expo in Cambodia this morning, June 29, 2018, Ms. Tek Reth Kamrong said, "The European Union is the first country to receive the most goods from Cambodia, especially in the field of clothing. "Bicycles and shoes, etc., which is to strengthen the relationship between Cambodia and Europe to be stronger."
She said that in 2017, the trade volume between Cambodia and the European Union was more than 6 billion dollars, of which Cambodia exported 4 billion dollars, while the European Union imported nearly 1 billion dollars. The European Union is the first country to receive Cambodia's exports.
It should be noted that on June 29, the European Union organized its first trade fair in Cambodia, with more than 40 companies participating, including companies, automobiles, furniture, consumer goods, machinery, medical equipment, medicine, financial services, food. Drinks and many other products.
Ms. Tek Reth Kamrong added that the EU exhibition today is a good opportunity for Cambodian and European investors to strengthen economic operations with other countries in the world. More importantly, this investment will not only benefit Cambodia, but will also benefit other countries in the world.
