Please note that on the night of April 7, 2015, Stung Treng Stone Market was on fire, causing complete damage and destruction of many traders' property.
Responding to the hardships of the business community, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit decided to build the Samaki Stung Treng Market and a stall for traders using Samdech's own budget and by the engineering forces of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The construction of Samaki Stung Treng market building and stalls was completed and completed on February 17, 2017, with 1,286 stalls and stone stalls for traders from rural areas selling 72 meters of fish and vegetables, equivalent to 623 traders. .
The provincial administration has arranged for the traders of Samaki Stung Treng Market to officially enter the market on March 15, 2017, because the new market has good design, good environment, comfortable electricity, water supply and security system, and each stall must Built in accordance with proper standards.
