(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presides over the groundbreaking ceremony for a new flyover and subway on Friday, June 29, 2018. Chom Chao, the sixth flyover in Phnom Penh.
This flyover and subway at Chom Chao roundabout is the sixth flyover in Phnom Penh after Kbal Thnal flyover, 7 Makara flyover, Stung Meanchey flyover, 5 Makara flyover and Phsar Dei Huy flyover, which is scheduled to be inaugurated in Phnom Penh. Early July.
The number of people, both permanent residents and those who come to do business, study and tourism is not less than 3 million people, while the number of vehicles has increased to more than 2 million, including registered bicycles. 1.5 million units and 600,000 vehicles of all types.
The rapid increase in the number of people and vehicles makes traffic in Phnom Penh more congested and congested, especially at roundabouts with multiple intersections. The Chom Chao roundabout is the intersection of several roads, including Russian Federation Boulevard, National Road 4, National Road 3 and Veng Sreng Road, which is currently causing heavy traffic congestion.
The construction of the flyover and subway at the Chom Chao roundabout is one of the Royal Government's efforts to solve the problems of the people in Phnom Penh, which takes a lot of time due to this traffic jam. The presence of flyovers and subways at the Chom Chao roundabout is expected to address these issues after completion.
Mr. Met Meas Pheakdey, Spokesman of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, said that the Choam Chao flyover is very important in solving the traffic congestion that has occurred in the past as well as now because this road is an economic road. Important for transportation to National Road No. 3 and National Road No. 4, which is a province with deep-sea ports in Cambodia to exchange goods in and out of the country.
He said that the bridge and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout is also an important economic route because it is the most important transportation network that allows investors, traders and the general public to benefit not only their own economy It saves time, but also saves people money.
The following is information related to the Chom Chao flyover and subway project:
Bridge 1: The main flyover connecting the traffic from the Boulevard of the Russian Federation to National Road No. 3, 408 meters long and 15.8 meters wide, with two lanes to two lanes to the bridge slope of 4.5 meters and a maximum height of Can travel under the bridge 5.5 meters.
Second Bridge: Separate from the main flyover, turn left and connect from the Boulevard of the Russian Federation to Veng Sreng Road for one-way traffic with one lane for cars and one lane for motorcycles with a total length of 202 meters (40 meters of flyover, subway) 118 meters long and 44 meters long dirt road) 5.25 meters wide.
