BANGKOK: Thai rescuers are using heavy machinery to drill into the walls of a mountain to speed up drainage from a cave where a total of 13 children, players and their coaches were trapped. The Tham Luong cave in Chiang Rai province has been in operation since last Saturday. This is according to the release by Thai Nation on Thursday night, June 28, 2018.
A total of 13 young players and coaches have been missing in the cave for the past five days, with experts believing they have penetrated deep into the cave. At a depth of 10 km, the road they had to return to was flooded after heavy rains.
