(Phnom Penh): Recently, the students and the President of the Student Association of Toul Kork Branch and Phsar Kandal Branch of ELT Primary and Secondary School held a commemoration ceremony for teachers and the transfer of the new President of the Student Association.
This program is conducted by students in order to thank the second benefactor, who he always teaches and mentors them throughout the whole school year, as well as to elect the president of the student association in each branch.
In this program, the students also expressed their gratitude to the teachers for their attention and guidance.
The selection and transfer ceremony of the President of the Student Association is also held every end of the school year to be a force to encourage ELT School students to work as a team, create programs and bring real experience and knowledge to them He. Meanwhile, the school has appointed three student representatives in each branch, which are listed below:
First: Toul Kork Branch * President of Cheam Andy Student Association * Vice President of Vibol Suyanut Student Association * Vice President of Sao Ly Heng Student Association
It should be noted that ELT Primary and Secondary School is an institution of ELT Education, which has been operating since 1994 and is recognized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and has a partnership with schools in other countries. A lot.
With more than 24 years of experience, ELT Primary and Secondary School has a national and international curriculum from Kindergarten to Grade 12 with highly qualified pedagogical teachers and well-equipped classrooms and laboratories. Modern facilities make it easy to study comfortably.
(Phnom Penh): The murder of a moneylender in Meanchey district was investigated by the Police Department of the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police until they arrested three perpetrators, including two couples.
On the morning of June 29, 2018, a police force led by Mr. Chiv Vibol, Director of the Office of Serious Crimes of the Ministry of Interior, brought the three perpetrators to show the location where they dumped their bodies into the canal water on the street. Meanchey District Hall. A report from Fresh News Agency, which was covering the incident, said that prior to the incident, the assailant had lent money from the victim but did not pay and was even searching for the victim. .
A disabled woman who raised nearly 10 children and grandchildren was fined 47 million for transporting used timber from Pursat province
(Kandal): A poor and disabled woman sitting alone in a wheelchair, Ms. Vong Theary, 51 years old, living in the village of Limestone, Slang, Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, said that due to lack of money, she had to raise four children and three grandchildren. Decided to buy wood or used wood to throw to the wood depot in Saang district, Kandal province, just to make a small profit to support daily life.
However, on June 22, 2018, the Forestry Administration and Kandal provincial authorities seized his rental car and required him to pay a fine of up to 47 million riels before returning the vehicle. Therefore, the disabled woman insisted that the timber administration officials be understanding because she did not have to announce the amount, if there was so much money, she would not be forced to buy used wood to feed her children Nearly 10 grandchildren.
The woman described that the reason why she was disabled was because her husband beat her so badly that she lost her unborn child while undergoing surgery for her injuries and became disabled to this day.
Due to the lack of livelihood, he decided to ask the governor of Pursat province and related skills to buy some used and good wood to sell to the timber depot in Saang district, lest he earn a little more profit to go to foot surgery and save some money for care. Children and grandchildren.
The disabled woman continued that because the provincial governor checked her condition, she was also allowed to buy and transport from Pursat province with the approval of the relevant experts. But for this transport, he asked to transport only three legs, with one foot of wood only 10 cubic meters. These trees are 12 and 15 times better quality wood, and he owed the depot owner almost all the money, giving the depot owner only $ 300, because he knew the owner of the depot.
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin has announced that the Russian military will upgrade its weapons by 2021, reaching 70 percent of its total. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday morning, June 29, 2018.
According to Vladimir Putin, the modernization of modern weapons in Russia's armed forces is now 60 percent complete, and the Russian strongman is expected to be the second largest military power in Russia. He will achieve his goal of 70% by 2021.
In addition, Putin said that the number of modern military equipment and weapons in the Russian army now is close to 60 percent, while six years ago, Russia has less than 16 percent of new and advanced weapons. However, in its ranks, this shows that in just six years, the Russian army has developed the most powerful weapons.
Russia has been actively modernizing its military equipment and weapons in recent years. According to Russia's military plan for 2018 to 2027, Moscow plans to spend $ 318 billion to upgrade military equipment and weapons.
A nun commits suicide at Wat Anteak in Battambang province due to depression, chronic illness
This incident happened at 17:30 on June 28, 2018 in the living room of Wat Andek in Krapeu Cheung village, Phnom Sampov commune, Banan district, Battambang province.
Mr. Mer Chhengly, Chief of Phnom Sampov Commune Administrative Police Station, said that the nun was a widow with one child named Tot Nhor, 65 years old, born in Koh Teav Village, Sampov Loun Commune, Koh Thom District, Kandal Province. Vegan at this turtle pagoda for more than 20 years, but due to a chronic illness, he decided to commit suicide.
